    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26071" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Laurētum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lōrētum</span></b> ), i,
			n.
		laurus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a laurel-grove</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tale,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Galb. 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Esp., <i>Lauretum</i> or <i>Laurel-grove</i>, a place on the Aventine Hill, <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 152</span></i>
			Müll.—Form Loretum, <i><span class="en">Plin. 15,
				30, 40, § 138</span></i>.</div>
